cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "foldrescue: pair-level prediction of pharmacological chaperone rescue"
message: >-
  If you use this software, please cite it. Note that the shipped demonstration
  results are produced on SYNTHETIC data and must not be cited as experimental
  or benchmark findings.
type: software
authors:
  - name: "foldrescue contributors"
repository-code: "https://github.com/xX-its-amit-Xx/foldrescue"
license: GPL-3.0-or-later
version: 0.1.0.dev0
date-released: "2026-10-10"
keywords:
  - pharmacological chaperone
  - missense variant
  - protein stability
  - probability calibration
  - applicability domain
  - conformal prediction
abstract: >-
  foldrescue predicts whether a given pharmacological chaperone rescues a given
  destabilising missense variant. Amenability is a property of a
  (variant, compound) pair: stability predictors answer whether a variant
  destabilises, and docking answers whether a ligand binds, but neither answers
  whether that binding rescues trafficking. foldrescue models the pair jointly
  across three model tiers (gradient-boosted trees over stability, structural
  and ligand features; frozen protein/chemical language model embeddings fused
  by cross-attention; and a structure-aware tier adding pocket-occupancy
  features), and treats probability calibration and applicability-domain
  reporting as primary outputs rather than diagnostics. Predictions outside the
  training distribution are flagged and are not ranked alongside supported
  predictions without an explicit opt-in. The package is intended for assay
  prioritisation research only and is not clinical decision support.
